PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real Terms & Conditions VC at static/gaia-x/tandc.jwt

Self-signed with the same key as legal-person.jwt. Single line <header>.<payload>.<signature>.

Payload (the VC), Loire / v2 shape:

{
  "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/credentials/v2", "https://w3id.org/gaia-x/development#"],
  "type": ["VerifiableCredential", "gx:Issuer"],
  "id": "https://YOUR_DOMAIN/gaia-x/tandc.jwt",
  "issuer": "did:web:YOUR_DOMAIN",
  "credentialSubject": {
    "id": "https://YOUR_DOMAIN/gaia-x/tandc.jwt#cs",
    "gaiaxTermsAndConditions": "4bd7554097444c960292b4726c2efa1373485e8a5565d94d41195214c5e0ceb3"
  }
}

FROM THE WIZARD instead: after 'Download all credentials' you get credentials.zip.
This credential is inside it as  Terms and conditions.jwt
The format is automatic (.jwt for anything signed) - there is nothing to choose.
RENAME it to this file's name; the Wizard never publishes it to your host.

The hash is a fixed constant per Trust Framework release. The value above is what the
GAIA-X Registry itself used as of 2026-09-15.
